Package: stareal
Title: Space-Time Areal Models Fitted on the Observed Cells Only
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Robert", "Verity", , "r.verity@imperial.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Bayesian space-time models for binomial survey data on a set of
    areal units (e.g. administrative units) and a regular time grid. The latent
    field is separable: a Leroux conditional autoregressive prior in space and
    a first-order autoregressive prior in time, plus fixed effects and a
    cell-level nugget. Because the prior is Gaussian, the unobserved area-time
    cells are integrated out exactly, so the model is fitted on the observed
    cells only. The full area-by-time table is then reconstructed by
    conditional simulation, one surface per posterior draw, and aggregated
    draw by draw to coarser groupings.
